# Drafted by `ctrm init` from the tracked files. Review it before you
# commit it: every grant is a decision. A pattern with no `/` matches a
# file name at any depth; the last matching line wins; a path no line
# matches gets `ascii`. `ctrm explain <path>` says which line decides.

# 97 text files read, 0 skipped (binary or not UTF-8).
# Pure ASCII, no line needed: *.json (2) *.jsonl (6) *.lock (2)
#   *.nix (1) *.rs (55) *.sh (1) *.txt (2) .context-ratchet (1)
#   .coverage (1) .envrc (1) .gitignore (1) LICENSE (1)

# *.md, files: 11.
# `spec-math` in `.ctrm-sets` covers the two deliberate mathematical symbols;
# `zh` covers the Chinese characters used in the explanatory text.
# `ctrm fix` rewrites, no grant needed: U+2013 U+2014 U+2026
*.md ascii+caveman+typography+math+box+legal+spec-math+zh

# *.pkl, files: 2.
# box for U+2500 U+2502 U+2514 U+251C
# marks for U+2192
# `ctrm fix` rewrites, no grant needed: U+2014 U+2019
*.pkl ascii+box+marks

# *.toml, files: 6.
# Needs no grant.
# `ctrm fix` rewrites, no grant needed: U+2014

# *.yml, files: 2.
# caveman for U+00B7
*.yml ascii+caveman

# .context-limits, files: 1.
# caveman for U+00A7
.context-limits ascii+caveman

# .spec-records, files: 1.
# caveman for U+22A5
# zh for U+6587 U+8A00
.spec-records ascii+caveman+zh
